---
import { AGENDA } from "../../lib/contact";
import StudioLayout from "../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro";
import Svg from "../../components/studio/Svg.astro";
---
<StudioLayout
  titre={'Software publishers and recurring services'}
  description={'Handle incoming requests, and above all bring their volume down at the source.'}
  actif="service-client">
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="ico"><Svg nom="demande-repetee" icone /></span>Software publishers, recurring services, B2B distribution</p>
    <h1>Answering faster isn&rsquo;t enough. The request has to stop coming.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Your team handles the same requests every week. Off-the-shelf tools offer to help you answer them faster. None of them tells you why they keep coming.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>What we put in place</h2>
    <p>An agent that qualifies each request, directs it to the right person, and answers the cases already handled.</p>
    <p>And every month, a report that groups requests by reason, costs them in volume and time spent, and identifies what is causing them upstream. <strong>Those causes are what we fix next.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="diagramme explicatif">
      <div class="d-large"><Svg nom="explicatif-service" /></div>
      <div class="d-etroit"><Svg nom="explicatif-service-portrait" /></div>
      <figcaption>Requests are grouped by cause. Once a cause is fixed, the requests it produced stop arriving.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>What we measure</h2>
    <ul class="measures">
      <li>Monthly request volume</li>
      <li>Share of repetitive requests</li>
      <li>Total time spent by the team</li>
      <li>Volume that disappears once the causes are fixed</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:26px">It&rsquo;s the last line we care about.</p>

    <p class="muted" style="font-size:14px;margin-top:2em">This case is built from situations observed in the industry. The orders of magnitude are assumptions until we measure them at your company.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Does this case look like yours?</h2>
    <p>45 minutes to find out whether this case costs you enough to be worth dealing with. If it doesn&rsquo;t, we&rsquo;ll tell you.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href={AGENDA} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/en/use-cases/">See the other cases</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</StudioLayout>
